## Useful Code Snippets

### Empty State View
```swift
ContentUnavailableView(
    "No Items",
    systemImage: "tray",
    description: Text("Add your first item to get started")
)
```

### Search with SwiftData
```swift
@Query private var items: [Item]
@State private var searchText = ""

var filteredItems: [Item] {
    if searchText.isEmpty {
        return items
    }
    return items.filter { $0.name.localizedCaseInsensitiveContains(searchText) }
}
```

### Confirmation Dialog
```swift
.confirmationDialog("Delete Item?", isPresented: $showDeleteConfirmation) {
    Button("Delete", role: .destructive) {
        deleteItem()
    }
}
```

---

## When Generating Code

1. **Always import necessary frameworks** (SwiftUI, SwiftData)
2. **Use iOS 26 APIs** - Don't use deprecated patterns
3. **Follow the established patterns** in the codebase
4. **Keep accessibility in mind** from the start
5. **Provide meaningful comments** for complex logic
6. **Use Preview providers** for all views

